# the entry of a tagged maker that makes `this` picks the layout by the tag, once for the whole program: one switch, one allocation for each layout, and the objects meet in front of the call of the body
# RUN: walk f1:AllocatingConstructEntry mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:AllocatingConstructEntry
# CHECK: = GetConstructPrototype
# CHECK: Switch {{*}}cases=[1, 2, 3, 4]
# CHECK: = NewObject
# CHECK: = NewObject
# CHECK: = NewObject
# the read of the prototype object stands once, in front of the switch
# RUN(ONCE): walk f1:AllocatingConstructEntry mechanisms=all
# ONCE: = GetConstructPrototype
# ONCE-NOT: = GetConstructPrototype
# RUN(WITHHELD): walk f1:AllocatingConstructEntry mechanisms=all-TypedSlots
# WITHHELD-LABEL: code f1:AllocatingConstructEntry
# WITHHELD-NOT: Switch
# WITHHELD: = NewObject {{*}}layout=L0
# WITHHELD-NOT: = NewObject
# PROGRAM-OF: ../typed-slots/new-with-a-known-tag-makes-the-member.ir
